  "prompt": "`MultiParser` does not instantiate the `MultiParser.Node` class.\n\nOn the `tip`:\n\nhttps://github.com/celery/celery/blob/8c753d7febd3be4e56cb0fda78b0704130a85299/celery/apps/multi.py#L307\n\n`MultiParser` defines a class variable `Node` (by default assigned to the default `Node` implementation), presumably for subclasses to easily customize which Node is instantiated by the parser.\n\nHowever, it seems the `MultiParser._node_from_options()` method always instantiates a default `celery.apps.multi.Node`, disregarding `MultiParser.Node`.\n\nCould we change this to use the `MultiParser.Node` class instead?\n\n```python\nreturn self.Node(nodename, cmd, append,\n                 p.optmerge(namespace, options), p.passthrough)\n```\n\nI am happy to submit a patch if this seems reasonable.",
